{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Remove living rooms from overcrowding standards in Housing Act 1985",
        "additional_details": "We believe the current statutory overcrowding standard is 40 years old and broken. We feel it allows landlords to count a family\u2019s only living room as a bedroom on paper to bypass overcrowding thresholds. This can force vulnerable and non-vulnerable families living in social housing to lose their only communal area.\r\n\r\nNo modern family should be trapped in bedrooms day and night with nowhere to eat, relax, or spend time together. We want the law to be modernised to protect all families facing this.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to amend Part X of the Housing Act 1985 to state that a household\u2019s living room cannot be legally counted as a bedroom space when calculating overcrowding space standards.",
